  "text": "Creating AFK Methods\nNote: This editor guide applies to AFK bossing, not slayer or low-effort methods.\n​\nGet your priorities straight\nAFK methods must:\n\n\nBe safe (rare chance of death)\n\n\nBe consistent (every hour is similar)\n\n\nBe easy to follow (no questions needed in #pvm-help)\n\n\n​\nAFK methods may:\n\n\nEncourage maximum KPH\n\n\nRequire minimum gear\n\n\nHave low upkeep costs\n\n\n​\nBuilding an AFK setup\nNote: This section only applies to AFK bossing - not AFK slayer.\n​\nThere are a couple of things to note:\n⬥ Abilities should ideally be fired in the exact same order every kill\n⬥ Some bosses take longer than others to start a fight\n​\nYou can improve consistency by reducing RNG:\n⬥ Removing critical strike boosters, e.g.,  /  / \n⬥ Disable pocket slot books  / \n​\nYou can make kill times slower by:\n⬥ downgrading prayers, e.g.,  →  → nothing\n⬥ removing extra-DPS gear/items, e.g.,  / \n⬥ downgrading gear, e.g.,  →  → \n⬥ downgrading spells / ammo\n​\nYou can make kill times faster by doing the opposite, plus:\n⬥ adding poison, e.g.,  / \n⬥ adding a DPS familiar, e.g., \n​\nSometimes during testing, two people have different results. Try this first to identify the differences (tag @Editing Staff if you can't figure it out or get into a disagreement and need support):\n⬥ Share screenshots of your buff bar, worn equipment, perks and familiar window\n​\nBreaking the bar: an example of AFK method writing\nSometimes, our bar \"breaks\" during testing and we need to adjust - let's walk through an example together and how we might solve it:\n⬥ The first ability is  (which has a 1-minute cooldown)\n⬥ You kill the boss at 28s, then wait another 27s for the next boss to respawn (\"fastest\" instance)\n⬥ The arena spawns the 2nd boss at 55s... and your  is still on cooldown... oops!\n​\nAt this point we should note - some bosses take longer than others to start the fight, so this might not be an issue. But let's assume for this example that the boss would have started attacking you immediately at the start of the fight.\n​\nYou have two options: remove  or try to slow down the kill by a few seconds. Let's do the latter!\n​\nThere are several ways to slow down a fight, and you can try any combination of these to find the sweet spot:\n⬥ If you are far off the mark, adjust the ability bar\n​\nIn our above  example:\n⬥ We're pretty close, so won't update the ability bar yet\n⬥ We will downgrade prayer from  → \n⬥ We will remove the \n⬥ We will switch from  to \n​\nEt voila! We are now up to consistent 30s kill times.\n      \n    ",
  "normalizedText": "Creating AFK Methods Note: This editor guide applies to AFK bossing, not slayer or low-effort methods. ​ Get your priorities straight AFK methods must: Be safe (rare chance of death) Be consistent (every hour is similar) Be easy to follow (no questions needed in #pvm-help) ​ AFK methods may: Encourage maximum KPH Require minimum gear Have low upkeep costs ​ Building an AFK setup Note: This section only applies to AFK bossing - not AFK slayer. ​ There are a couple of things to note: ⬥ Abilities should ideally be fired in the exact same order every kill ⬥ Some bosses take longer than others to start a fight ​ You can improve consistency by reducing RNG: ⬥ Removing critical strike boosters, e.g., / / ⬥ Disable pocket slot books / ​ You can make kill times slower by: ⬥ downgrading prayers, e.g., → → nothing ⬥ removing extra-DPS gear/items, e.g., / ⬥ downgrading gear, e.g., → → ⬥ downgrading spells / ammo ​ You can make kill times faster by doing the opposite, plus: ⬥ adding poison, e.g., / ⬥ adding a DPS familiar, e.g., ​ Sometimes during testing, two people have different results. Try this first to identify the differences (tag @Editing Staff if you can't figure it out or get into a disagreement and need support): ⬥ Share screenshots of your buff bar, worn equipment, perks and familiar window ​ Breaking the bar: an example of AFK method writing Sometimes, our bar \"breaks\" during testing and we need to adjust - let's walk through an example together and how we might solve it: ⬥ The first ability is (which has a 1-minute cooldown) ⬥ You kill the boss at 28s, then wait another 27s for the next boss to respawn (\"fastest\" instance) ⬥ The arena spawns the 2nd boss at 55s... and your is still on cooldown... oops! ​ At this point we should note - some bosses take longer than others to start the fight, so this might not be an issue. But let's assume for this example that the boss would have started attacking you immediately at the start of the fight. ​ You have two options: remove or try to slow down the kill by a few seconds. Let's do the latter! ​ There are several ways to slow down a fight, and you can try any combination of these to find the sweet spot: ⬥ If you are far off the mark, adjust the ability bar ​ In our above example: ⬥ We're pretty close, so won't update the ability bar yet ⬥ We will downgrade prayer from → ⬥ We will remove the ⬥ We will switch from to ​ Et voila! We are now up to consistent 30s kill times.",
